    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "У нас французский ресторан.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We have a French restaurant.' The key word here means 'us', which Chef Viktor combines with 'French'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А не японский.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And not Japanese.' Notice the word order: 'Japanese' comes first, and 'Japanese' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Я обожаю суши.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I adore sushi.' You'll hear 'I' all the time in the show, here connected with 'sushi'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Я ем их каждый день.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I eat them every day.' Notice the word order: 'I' comes first, and 'day' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "А если ты захочешь хачапури?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'And what if you want khachapuri?' You'll hear 'you' all the time in the show, here connected with 'khachapuri'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Я вызову хачапурщика.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will call a khachapuri maker.' The first content word means 'I', and 'khachapuri baker' rounds out the thought. Senya answers straight away.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Я умею готовить хачапури.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I know how to cook khachapuri.' A compact expression built around 'I' and 'khachapuri'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Заткнись и пошёл вон.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Shut up and get out.' Notice the word order: 'shut up' comes first, and 'went' finishes the sentence.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "С тобой невозможно разговаривать.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is impossible to talk to you.' The first content word means 'you', and 'to talk' rounds out the thought. Then Kristina replies.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Кстати, Вика у нас не работает.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'By the way, Vika doesn't work for us.' Kristina puts 'by the way' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'Vika'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Ты её уволила?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Did you fire her?' You'll hear 'you' all the time in the show, here connected with 'to fire'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "kristina",
      "t": "Она сама уволилась.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
